WebKit: the C API's content-rule-list notification also reports a load a list blocked.

WebPageProxy::contentRuleListNotification fires for every load a rule list blocked (the
WebProcess sends it when ContentRuleListResults::shouldNotifyApplication() holds, which includes
blockedLoad), but the C API wrapper in WKPage.cpp forwards only the strings of `notify` actions:
a blocked load with no `notify` rule reaches the embedder as nothing. LazyWeb+'s ad blocker
(issue #845) wants the number of loads it stopped on the page, and a `notify` duplicate of every
`block` rule would double the compiled list for it. The wrapper now appends one entry per list
that blocked the load, with the notification string "lazyos:blocked", so the navigation client's
contentRuleListNotification callback sees the load. A rule list that uses `notify` for something
else is unaffected (its own strings come first, unchanged).

--- a/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/API/C/WKPage.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebKit/UIProcess/API/C/WKPage.cpp
@@ -2515,6 +2515,12 @@
                     apiListIdentifiers.append(API::String::create(listIdentifier));
                     apiNotifications.append(API::String::create(notification));
                 }
+                // LazyOS: a load a rule list blocked is reported too, as "lazyos:blocked", so the
+                // browser can count what its ad blocker stopped without a `notify` rule per block.
+                if (result.blockedLoad) {
+                    apiListIdentifiers.append(API::String::create(listIdentifier));
+                    apiNotifications.append(API::String::create("lazyos:blocked"_s));
+                }
             }
 
             if (!apiNotifications.isEmpty())
